# Per-server settings: copy to proxy/config.env and adapt. Without this file CF
# uses 127-0-0-1.nip.io and is reachable only on the server itself.
# After a change: make -f Makefile.proxy down host-setup up

# The server address that other machines use. The domain follows from it,
# e.g. 192.168.10.182 gives 192-168-10-182.nip.io.
#CF_HOST_IP=192.168.10.182

# Optional: your own domain instead of nip.io. It needs a wildcard DNS entry
# *.<domain> pointing to CF_HOST_IP, which must be set as well.
#CLUSTER_DOMAIN=cf.example.internal
